; THE KESTREL — 0.28 m, 0.65 kg, TWR 4.5. A 5-inch RC quad, and the roster's
; DATUM in every sense: P3.4 defines its whole balance column as zeros, and since
; 2026-08-10 it is also the low end of the SIZE ladder (kestrel / condor / roc).
;
; It was briefly overwritten with the 3 m aircraft's numbers while phase 2 was
; being built. Those numbers now live in `default_flight_roc.tres` and this file
; is back to exactly what it was on `master` — bit for bit, plus the two fields
; the size ladder added. **That restoration is load-bearing:** the whole point of
; flying the Kestrel in the scale yard is to feel the world be ten times larger
; around the machine you already know, and a Kestrel with the Roc's TWR would not
; be that machine.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="FlightConfig" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://resources/flight_config.gd" id="1_cfg"]

[resource]
